CHAPTER.VERS:
Thus says Yahweh: Execute

          {+}
         justice and righteousness, and deliver him who is robbed out of the hand of the oppressor: and do no wrong, do no violence, to the sojourner, the fatherless, nor the widow; neither shed innocent blood in this place.

For if you

          {+}
         do this thing indeed, then there will enter in by the gates of this house kings sitting on the throne of David, riding in chariots and on horses, he, and his slaves, and his people.

But if you

          {+}
         will not hear these words, I swear by myself, says Yahweh, that this house will become a desolation.

Don't weep

          {+}
         for the dead, neither bemoan him; but weep intensely for him who goes away; for he will return no more, nor see his native country.

And I will cast you out, and your mother who bore you, into another country, where you

          {+}
         were not born; and there you

          {+}
         will die.

Thus says Yahweh, Write

          {+}
         this man childless, a [prominent] man who will not prosper in his days; for no more will a man of his seed prosper, sitting on the throne of David, and ruling in Judah.
